# AI Integration with Ollama and LangChain

## Ollama Client Implementation
Based on [ollamaClient.js](mdc:backend/src/infrastructure/ollamaClient.js):

### Client Configuration
```javascript
constructor(baseUrl = "http://localhost:11434", model = "openchat:latest", streaming = true) {
    this.model = new ChatOllama({
        baseUrl,
        model,
        streaming: streaming,
        temperature: 1,
    });
}
```

### LangChain Integration
- Use `ChatPromptTemplate` for prompt management
- Use `MessagesPlaceholder` for chat history
- Use `RunnableSequence` for chaining operations
- Format messages with proper LangChain message types

### Message Formatting Pattern
```javascript
formatMessages(chatHistory) {
    return chatHistory.map(msg => {
        switch (msg.role) {
            case 'human': return new HumanMessage(msg.content);
            case 'ai': return new AIMessage(msg.content);
            case 'system': return new SystemMessage(msg.content);
            default: return new HumanMessage(msg.content);
        }
    });
}
```

## Chat Service Integration
Based on [chatService.js](mdc:backend/src/application/chatService.js):

### Streaming Response Handling
```javascript
async sendMessageSSE(userInput, onMessage) {
    const response = await this.ollamaClient.sendMessageSSE(
        this.chatHistory.getMessages(),
        userInput
    );
    
    let fullResponse = '';
    for await (const chunk of response) {
        const content = chunk.content || '';
        fullResponse += content;
        onMessage({ type: 'ai', content });
    }
    
    this.chatHistory.addMessage('ai', fullResponse);
    return fullResponse;
}
```

